or players, and that the abundance of healing definately has something to do with that. 40-60 gold per HP for a carried is not unreasonable, howeverwe need to look at how that balances with guild regenerative abilitiesas well.  Once we limit the availability of portable healing, suddenlyany guild that offers healing is considerably more potent.  I think if we do things like this that we should perhaps balance meditation skillswith something like 'can only meditate in a temple'... with that being just one example.W.**redsexy**To: kryllSubj: Cantina ReportsDate: Oct 29OK everything has been changed apart from three things...1)  WC of Snips.  They're meant to be like kickass mosquitos,  capable of killing people quickly but dead easy to kill  I'll change that if u like.2)  Only finding one jar.  I hate it when people can just keep   on finding stuff by searching over and over. There   is no need for anyone to be walking around with more  than one jar, so I set it to just the one.3)  Variable experience on table.  I'll wait til you've   looked into it, but the idea of winning experience  from gambling is already in the game... see Wilbie's   Wheel of Fortune.  I think the odds are pretty   even for winning and loosing....I've done a bit of the desert, but I'll do most of thattomorrow.  I'll also need u to help me figure why d5doesn't load 1st try....Thanks, and see ya soon,=Red**sauron**To: airborneRe:   healingCc: archesDate: Oct 31I don't know that we should remove all meditation outside of a 'temple' butmaybe we could reduce the healing rate outside of that player's guild rooms.Seems to me that being in their temple, or at their shrine, or whatever,should heal them faster, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: kryllFwd:  healingCc: archesDate: Nov  1To: airborneRe:   healingCc: archesDate: Oct 31I don't know that we should remove all meditation outside of a 'temple' butmaybe we could reduce the healing rate outside of that player's guild rooms.Seems to me that being in their temple, or at their shrine, or whatever,should heal them faster, or conversely, being away from there should healthem slower (since we want to reduce the healing, not increase it).Dave**airborne**To: kryllSubj: healing...Cc: archesDate: Nov  1Sorry about that, zigged when I should have zagged.Here's the idea that I have been bouncing about in my head.  Ok, suppose we limit meditation/healing skills to only the guild roomand \"shrines\".  Then we give guild members the ability to create shrines in various locations.  Players will be able to have their healing, but they would have to work a bit for it.  To start, we'd have the shrine needed to be built.  An easy way toget players to spend a bunch of gold on all sorts of things, bowls, statues, insense, etc.  Then they would have to protect those locationsonce they were built.  Certainly leaving lots of valuables laying around would tempt almost any player, which would kinda be the point.Add in the idea that some elements of theshrine would degrade withtime (insence comes to mind) and have to be replaced every so often.  The idea is to create an economy by finding reasons for players to gatheror purchase things that aren't just for killing.  If insence were onlyavailable in a small handful of locations, and there was a demand for itwe'd create the demand.  It helps control healing rates, keeps moneydown a bit, adds a roleplaying element to the mud, and encourages guildsto work together.Ideas and critics?**mangla**To: tatsuoSubj: arenaCc: exos, archesDate: Mar 19I had another though. If we get enough people. I would notmind seeing two arena a day when it makes sense. But thesecond arena would be open for lower levels. So be carefulwhen opening the arenas, and if there are more lower levels