 its calledIrish Luck.  Luck can account for a lot of things, including avoiding an attack you do not see coming.  While the message this dodgereturns may not be descriptive of the attack,that does not disqualify it.After all, as a player, I have pounded skeletons into a pile of bloodand body parts many times.The message may be innaccurate, but the effect is the same.**brainsprain**To: turboSubj: in reply to bothCc: archesDate: Apr  8Yeah, arches will mail all of the arches, i think wizzes works as wellto send to everybody.As to to skill or spell, that is fine, what happened was malice and treatwere in the arena and I was watching the battle over malices shoulder.I watched treat sidestep a backstab, which made no sense whatsoever to me.  When i asked him how he did ithe refused to cooperate, so i asked him if it was a skill, and if it wasthat it would suffice, he told me it was a skill, so i asked him what that skill was, he wouldn't tell me (telling me, of course, would havessettled this without you and I even having to discuss it, I think this is,btw, a very valid skill.  Thanks for the info, i wont be coding around the spell, i think it is very valid,but I do have one question: What level does a bard have to bein order to get that skill and does it take the attackers levelinto account, I think it should, that way lvl 22 bards arent dodging attacksfrom L10 thieves (just an example).  Thanks turboThe sprain**brainsprain**To: kryllSubj: First goldsun areaCc: archesDate: Apr 14I have revised the first of goldsun's area .. the poorly named7-islands (since there are only 6)  However, I have my ownarea, a huge island, that i am going to rebuild into the 7th island.  That aside, I would like to get the area putinto play as soon as possible, it is in:/players/brainsprain/goldsun/7-islands/**"
